  "details": "StateMachineBehaviours have OnEnter, OnExit, and OnUpdate as built in callbacks. Currently, we only get OnEnter behavior with the current implementation of state behaviors in VRChat.\n\nIt would be great to have the ability to choose when our state behaviors fire- when entering the state (OnEnter) and when exiting a state (OnExit). This would help cut down on bloated state machines and simplify advanced 3.0 logic. \n\nAn example could be a state that you’d like to have IK disabled for only while in that specific state. Using OnEnter to disable, and OnExit to reenable, you wouldn’t need to add a parameter driver to every possible state afterwards to make sure your logic doesn’t break when exiting. This is especially important for setups that can transition anywhere using AnyState, or may use a combination of behaviors elsewhere that mix into the logic. Incorporating into parameter drivers would also be incredibly useful for things that may need to be set while in a state, and reverted or changed when exiting that state.\n\nThere are plenty of advantages to having access to OnExit as an option for our state behaviors that i’m sure the community would benefit from having access to.\n\nAs part of one of my own projects, I built my own parameter driver script and incorporated this feature as an option. At first I only played with it for testing, but further on I became heavily reliant on it and how much it cut down bloated logic. I am confident that the same would apply here.",
